    "body": "## Summary\n\nTwo post-ADR-018 housekeeping items; no code changes.\n\n**`CHANGELOG.md`** (new) -- Keep-a-Changelog format. `[Unreleased]` section documents ADR-018's user-visible changes (state pseudo-classes, click navigation) plus the infrastructure additions and the use-after-free fix. `[0.4.0]` section notes the current baseline release; prior history lives in git log and `docs/decisions/`.\n\n**`docs/README.md`** (new) -- orients readers to the material under `docs/`. Sections for guides, decisions, learning, recruitment, plus an explicit \"Manual test fixtures\" list naming the eight HTML test pages in this directory, one line each with what they verify and which ADR introduced them.\n\n## Why not move the fixtures?\n\nThe original plan was to move `docs/link-test-*.html` -> `tests/fixtures/`. The diagnostic revealed `docs/` is already the informal fixture directory -- there are five other test HTML files there (`dir-test.html`, `inline-test.html`, `inline-color-test.html`, `wrap-test.html`, plus `demo.html`). Moving only the three `link-test-*` files creates a *split* fixture directory, which is worse than the status quo.\n\nThe right sequence is:\n\n1. **Document current state** (this PR) -- `docs/README.md` names the fixtures and their purpose.\n2. **Consolidate later** (future PR) -- move all 8-9 HTML test files together, once the diagnostic pass confirms none are referenced from markdown or screenshots.\n\n## Not in scope\n\n- No code changes\n- No file moves\n- No test changes\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `cmake --build build` clean\n- `./build/tests/honeybee_tests` -- 237 cases, 905 assertions, all pass\n- No source touched, so no test changes required\n\nRefs #136\n",
